  "question": "Does the exact Godot/Jolt active-step-snapshot v2 runtime profile satisfy every previously declared R24D3 mechanism-coverage prerequisite needed to promote its solved motor-impulse and dependent actuator-work channels into the exact-s169 R24 recovery capability mapping?",
  "answer": "No. R24D10 validly characterized the complete frozen fixture and positively exposed signed drive impulse, positive motor work, hard-cap behavior, disabled-motor zero, limit separation, refusal, and freshness. Its two intended signed-braking cells reported exactly zero motor impulse and zero absorbed motor work, identical in those motor telemetry fields to the paired disabled cells. The previously declared absorbed-work mechanism therefore has no native witness, so the instrumented profile remains unpromoted.",
