    "mechanism_witness_rule": "Each signed-braking direction must contain at least one current native sample with strictly positive absorbed_motor_work_j, strictly negative net_motor_work_j, and a nonzero signed_motor_impulse_nms opposing the declared nonzero initial canonical rate. A zero result is not failed performance; it means the required mechanism was not activated and therefore was not characterized.",
    "adequacy_argument": "R24D3 required positive and absorbed motor-work characterization before any instrumented-profile promotion. Exact nonzero directionality is a source-derived mechanism-activation witness, not an empirical locomotion-performance threshold or fitted numerical tolerance. The complete R24D10 record is adequate to decide whether that mechanism appeared in its finite fixture. It is not adequate to infer why the mechanism was absent, accept numerical accuracy, generalize to arbitrary hinges, or promote the profile despite the missing witness. Refusal is therefore the only decision consistent with the previously declared requirement and the immutable observed record."
